  "body": "Found by the delta read of PR #3308 (head `b0efe2ee6`). The code has no caller at this time. Fix this before a command or a pattern uses `PreserveClimb`.\n\n## What happens\n\n`leads_match` (`crates/cl/src/cl/transform_climb.rs:122-126`) accepts a pass when its first and its last planar move have the same shape and the same length (2 um). It does not check that the last move is a lead-out.\n\nExample: a 5 mm linear lead-in, a closed contour whose last edge is a 5 mm straight, and no lead-out. The check accepts the pass. After the mirror and the reversal, the plunge is on the contour at full depth.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe reversal refuses, by name, a pass whose reversed plunge point is on the cut contour. Options: the generator marks the lead moves in the path, or the caller states that the leads are symmetric.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test pins the example above as a refusal.\n- The decision file `docs/decisions/3011-cl-transforms.md` names the rule.\n\nRefs #3011.\n",
